# Sinfonia 14 in B-flat major, BWV 800 (4/4, 24 bars)
#
# Character: warm, lyrical and ornate. A short subject (a held note,
# a falling sixteenth turn, a dotted-sounding cadence figure) treated in
# close imitation, with florid sixteenth and thirty-second lines. Calm,
# singing, unhurried.
#
# Tempo: quarter = 72, about 1:20.
# Basis: Angela Hewitt (Hyperion, 1994) 1:18, about 74; Andras Schiff
# (ECM, clavichord) 1:18, about 74; Glenn Gould (1964) 1:09, about 83.
# A touch under Hewitt and Schiff for the thirty-seconds in bar 23.
# Durations from retailer and artist track lists, so approximate.
#
# Structure (from the Mutopia score):
#   1      Subject in the mid, B-flat major, over a walking bass.
#   2      Answer in the top, on F.
#   4      Subject in the bass, B-flat major; falling sequence in 5.
#   7      Arrival back on B-flat; subject in the mid turning to
#          G minor (7), answer in the top in C minor (8).
#   10     Cadence in C minor; subject in the bass (10).
#   12-14  Subject in the top toward D minor; cadence in D minor, 14.
#   14-19  Episode through G minor, C minor and E-flat.
#   20-21  Return to B-flat: subject in the mid (20) and in the top
#          (20, second half), close together.
#   22-24  Closing bars over a broken bass; florid run in 23; final
#          cadence in B-flat major.
# The cadence points in 7, 10, 14 and 20 are my reading of the score;
# I found no published analysis to confirm them.

tempo 72 4

dyn 1 mp              # bars 1-6: exposition, quiet and singing
lead 1 mid            # bar 1: subject in the mid
lead 2 top            # bar 2: answer in the top, on F
lead 4 bottom         # bar 4: subject in the bass

dyn 7 mf              # bars 7-14: after the return to B-flat, entries toward the minor keys
lead 7 mid            # bar 7: subject in the mid, turning to G minor
lead 8 top            # bar 8: answer in the top, C minor
lead 10 bottom        # bar 10: subject in the bass after the C minor cadence
lead 12 top           # bar 12: subject in the top, toward D minor

dyn 15 mp             # bars 15-19: episode after the D minor cadence, a softer manual

dyn 20 f              # bars 20-24: the subject returns in the home key
lead 20 mid           # bar 20: subject in the mid, B-flat
lead 20.5-21 top      # bars 20-21: subject in the top, from the middle of bar 20

rit 2 0.7             # last 2 bars: the florid run and the final chord
